      ],
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>This is in my <a href=\"http://www.spiffworld.com/sotm/files/sotm_rules_and_clarifications.pdf\">FAQ</a>.&nbsp; It talks about Tempest&#39;s &quot;Cleansing Downpour&quot;, but it&#39;s essentially the same situation and has been confirmed by the developers:</p><blockquote><p>Duplicate Powers<br />If a card is not Limited, you can have multiple copies of it in play. However,<br />each copy of the card is considered its own power. Since you are limited to<br />activating one power per turn, you may thus only activate one of the two<br />&ldquo;instances&rdquo; of the power during your power phase. For example:<br />If you have two copies of &ldquo;Cleansing Downpour&rdquo; (Tempest card) in play (which<br />reads &ldquo;Power: Each Hero regains 2 HP.&rdquo;), you can use either &ldquo;instance&rdquo; of the<br />power on your power phase, but in either case, the power will simply work as<br />written (i.e., each hero will regain 2 HP). If for any reason you can use an<br />additional power on your turn, you may opt to use a second &ldquo;instance&rdquo; of the<br />power on Cleansing Downpour since they come from different distinct cards.</p></blockquote>",
